  ### 3.3 Events, boundaries, gaps [V]
  `EEG.event(i).type` (string or number, keep homogeneous), `.latency` in **samples, 1-based, may be fractional** (eeg_insertbound.m header: "a latency of 2000.3 means 0.3 samples ... after the 2001st data frame (since first frame has latency 0)"), `.duration` (samples), `.urevent` (created by `eeg_checkset(EEG,'makeur')`), `.epoch`. eeg_checkset forces numeric event fields to double (537-560), removes events with latency < 0.5 or > pnts*trials+1 (429-432). Discontinuities: event type `'boundary'` (or `-99` when `option_boundary99` and numeric types; `eeg_boundarytype.m`, `eeg_isboundary.m`). `functions/popfunc/eeg_insertbound.m:115-117` verbatim:
  ```matlab
  eventin(end+1).type   = eeg_boundarytype(eventin);
  eventin(end).latency  = regions(iRegion,1)-sum(lengths(1:iRegion-1))-0.5;
  eventin(end).duration = lengths(iRegion,1)+addlength;
  ```
  i.e. boundary at half-sample between last sample before and first after the gap; `duration` = samples removed (NaN when unknown; bva-io sets `duration = NaN` for 'New Segment', pop_loadbv.m:437-439). eeg_checkset merges duplicate boundaries (adding durations) and drops a boundary beyond data end (521-545). **Recommended gap representation**: concatenate without padding, insert `type='boundary', latency=<samples before gap>+0.5, duration=<missing samples>`. Zero padding is never used by EEGLAB (eeg_eegrej, pop_mergeset, imports all use boundaries) [V conventions, I recommendation].
  EEGLAB's EDF importers: `pop_biosig` -> `biosig2eeglab.m` -> `functions/sigprocfunc/biosig2eeglabevent.m`: `latency = EVENT.POS`, `duration = EVENT.DUR`, type = `EVENT.TYP` or CodeDesc text when importannot and `eType > 255`; **EDF+ codes 32766/32767 mapped to boundary** (77-80: `if eType == 32766 || eType == 32767, event(index).edfplustype = event(index).type; event(index).type = eeg_boundarytype(event);`); pop_biosig appends `dat.EDFplus.*` vectors as extra channels (257-268), `eeg_checkset(EEG,'eventconsistency')` (297). `pop_fileio.m:395-407`: `type = event.value; value = event.type; latency = event.sample+offset+subsample; duration = event.duration` then removes sample/value/offset; **no boundary handling at all**. FieldTrip `ft_read_event.m` case 'edf' (743-783) parses EDF+ TAL annotations (`read_edf` + `tokenize(char(evt), char(0))`); EDF+D discontinuities not turned into boundaries [I]. `readedf.m` = legacy plain-EDF reader.

