  ## 4. File-IO (FieldTrip) and BioSig

  ### 4.1 pop_fileio [V]
  `pop_fileio.m` is **core** (`functions/popfunc/`, BSD-2), not part of the plugin. Header: "POP_FILEIO - import data files into EEGLAB using FileIO ... >> OUTEEG = pop_fileio( filename ); >> OUTEEG = pop_fileio( header, dat, evt ); 'dataformat' - [string] data format. Default is automatic. Available choices are available in ft_read_data ... Note: FILEIO toolbox must be installed." Flow: `if ~plugin_askinstall('Fileio', 'ft_read_data'), return; end` (64) -> `dat = ft_read_header(filename);` (105 GUI / 152 scripted; **no headerformat option, so header detection is purely ft_filetype**) -> `'dataformat'` forwarded only if not 'auto' (199) -> `ft_read_data(filename,'header',dat,dataopts{:})` (203) -> `ft_read_event(filename, dataopts{:})` (382). GUI lists ~100 hard-coded format names (91-100). Fills `EEG.srate = dat.Fs; EEG.nbchan = dat.nChans; EEG.data = alldata; EEG.setname=''; EEG.comments=['Original file: ' filename]; EEG.xmin = -dat.nSamplesPre/EEG.srate; EEG.trials = dat.nTrials;` (240-246), chanlocs labels/type/XYZ from dat.label/chantype/elec (258-345), `EEG.etc.fileio_dat = dat` (343).

  ### 4.2 The Fileio plugin [V/I]
  It is a dated snapshot of FieldTrip's fileio module: `eeglab.prj` lists `plugins/Fileio250523` and `plugins/Fieldtrip-lite250523` (+ `.../external/biosig`) (lines 123-130) = 2025-05-23 snapshots [V]. eeglab.m special-cases folders containing `fieldtrip` (adds compat/forward/utilities/plotting, removes external/*) and sets version 'ersion unknowned' for fieldtrip/fileio folders (1059-1091, 1116-1121) [V]. Wiki: "FileIO (https://github.com/fieldtrip/fileio): Toolbox allowing data import in multiple data formats" (EEGLAB_Extensions.md:136). fieldtrip/fileio repo = exactly the module (ft_read_header/data/event, ft_filetype, private/, GPL-3 COPYING); its log is "synchronized with main FieldTrip repository" commits (last ten 2026-06-24..2026-09-24) [V+W]. Repackaging is undocumented; naming `Fileio<yymmdd>` and the compile recipe ("Do not use the GIT version of FieldTrip ... Instead get the latest plugin", Compiled_EEGLAB.md:210-219) indicate SCCN uploads a snapshot around each ~annual release [I]. **Lag from FieldTrip merge to manager users: months to ~1 year**, unless users install FieldTrip itself [I].

  ### 4.3 Would a FieldTrip-side Cadwell reader auto-appear? [V]
  Only if `ft_filetype` recognises the file (pop_fileio passes no `headerformat`). `ft_read_header.m:17` "'headerformat' = name of a MATLAB function that takes the filename as input (default is automatic)"; line 44 "To use an external reading function, you can specify an external function as the 'headerformat' option ... search for BIDS_TSV as example"; ft_read_data (34) / ft_read_event accept function names for dataformat/eventformat. mffmatlabio uses exactly this hook (`mff_fileio_read_header.m` etc.) [V]. But pop_fileio only forwards `'dataformat'`, never headerformat, so the GUI needs ft_filetype support. `ft_filetype.m` (master 2026-09-28) has **no** cadwell/ezdata/sqlite detection (only `.easy` -> `neuroelectrics_easy`, 1290) [V]. So: a FieldTrip PR touching ft_filetype.m, ft_read_header/data/event.m + `private/read_cadwell_*.m`; a SQLite dependency (`sqlite()` = Database Toolbox R2022a+, or mksqlite MEX) would be a first for fileio [I]. ft_read_header also has `'fallback' = 'biosig'` (12) [V].

  ### 4.4 BioSig and Cadwell [V]
  pop_biosig -> sopen/sread from the Biosig plugin (eeglab.m:1095-1099 adds `<Biosig>/biosig/t200_FileAccess`). MATLAB `sopen.m` (two GitHub mirrors, 494-506 kB) has **no** cadwell/ezdata/EASY string [V; older mirrors, current GitLab blocked]. biosig4c++ has `t210/sopen_cadwell_read.c` (Copyright 2021 Alois Schloegl, GPL-3), comment "read CADWELL file formats (EAS, EZ3, ARC)"; all three branches end in `biosigERROR(hdr, B4C_FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED, "Format EAS(Cadwell): unsupported ")` / EZ3 / ARC (lines 92, 287, 291) - a reverse-engineering stub, plus sibling `sopen_sqlite.c` [V]. SourceForge feature request #13 "Support for AES, EZ3, and ARC fiile formats" (2021-08-27, open; comment 2021-09-30: "sopen_cadwell.c and sopen_sqlite.c are used to develop tools for reverse engineering") [W]. Nothing about `.ezdata`. BioSig cannot read Cadwell today.

  ---

  ## 5. MATLAB / Octave compatibility
  - Minimum MATLAB: `Contributing_to_EEGLAB.md:69` "MATLAB version 2008b or later is required; We recommend using the latest version". eeglab.m:204-220 refuses `vers < 7`, warns `< 7.06` ("older than 7.6 (2008a) ... Some of the EEGLAB functions might not be functional"); handles `> 24` (MATLAB Copilot buttons) [V]. No separate plugin minimum; mffmatlabio README: "will not work with version of Matlab older than 2014a as the Java JAR file cannot be properly interfaced" [V].
  - Octave: `Running_EEGLAB_on_Octave.md` (full text) [V]: "As of 2021, we are supporting the Octave ... environment (both command line calls and graphic interface)"; "not as stable ... first choice MATLAB, second compiled, third Octave"; "best tested using Octave 6.1 on Windows"; "**Plug-ins need to be installed manually** (downloaded as zip files and uncompressed in the EEGLAB plugins folder). Most plugins (including SIFT and LIMO) have not been tested on Octave and will likely not be functional"; ICLabel on Octave 8.4 "15+ hours ... compared to 10 seconds". eeglab.m: `pkg load statistics` when `~ismatlab`; plugin-install menus only `if ismatlab && ~nouiflag` (1210) [V]. CI runs an Octave smoke test every push. bva-io has an "Octave compatible code below" fallback (pop_loadbv.m:122) [V]. Revision history: "Improved Octave 8.4 compatibility", "Full Octave compatibility from the command line" (2019) [V].
  - MEX/Java: no wiki guidance (design_plugin.md, EEGLAB_Extensions.md, Contributing_to_EEGLAB.md contain no "mex"/"Java") [V]. Practice: **ANTeepimport1.14** ships `eepv4_read.mexa64/.mexmaci64/.mexw32/.mexw64` (+ _info, _version) in the plugin root (eeglab.prj:109-120) [V]; **xdfimport** ships `load_xdf_innerloop.c` + `.mexw64/.mexa64/.mexmaci64/.mexmaca64` in `xdf/`, readme "version 1.19 includes MATLAB binaries" [V+W]; **mffmatlabio** ships a 4.6MB jar and `javaaddpath(fullfile(p,'MFF-1.2.2-jar-with-dependencies.jar'))` in mff_path.m [V]; **Biosig** plugin bundles mexSLOAD (pop_biosig `'importmex'`) [V]. Manager just unzips; binaries must be pre-built for all platforms. Compiled EEGLAB cannot add plugins (Compiled_EEGLAB.md:132-134) [V]. For Cadwell: Database Toolbox `sqlite()` (R2022a+) vs bundled mksqlite MEX (4 platforms) vs Java sqlite-jdbc via javaaddpath (MATLAB only, not Octave) [I].

  ---

  ## 6. Testing conventions
  - Core CI `eeglab/.github/workflows/test.yml` (full text) [V]: push/PR to master/develop: `octave-smoke` (ubuntu, apt octave, `eeglab('nogui'); EEG = pop_loadset(...'eeglab_data.set'...); EEG = eeg_checkset(EEG); assert(EEG.nbchan == size(EEG.data,1)); assert(EEG.pnts == size(EEG.data,2));`) and `matlab-smoke` (`matlab-actions/setup-matlab@v2` R2024b, skipped without `MATLAB_BATCH_TOKEN`). Also `claude.yml`/`claude-code-review.yml` (Claude Code bot on @claude by owners/members). **No `test/` dir in the repo** [V].
  - Test repos [W]: https://github.com/sccn/eeglab_tests (README verbatim: "tests to validate correct behavior of EEGLAB. This repository uses ... MATLAB Projects, MATLAB Unit Testing, Git LFS, Git submodules and GitHub Actions"; `unittesting_*` incl. `unittesting_binary` for readers; `*wrapperTest.m` wrap legacy tests; `.github/workflows/ci.yml` matrix `release: [R2021b,R2025a]`, `matlab-actions/run-tests@v2`, codecov, dorny/test-reporter [V raw ci.yml]) and older https://github.com/sccn/eeglab-testcases (git-annex, runtest.m). Wiki `EEGLAB_test_cases.md`: "~5,000 test cases cover about 10% of all possible function call variations"; unittesting_binary "test cases for reading binary data files ... anonymized binary test data files (500 MB)" [V].
  - Plugins: none of bva-io, neuroscanio, xdf-EEGLAB, mffmatlabio, firfilt, clean_rawdata, ICLabel, EEG-BIDS has `.github/workflows` [V/W]. Convention: hand-run `test_*.m` in repo root. CONTRIBUTING.md asks core PRs for test scripts and to "add the test case to the EEGLAB test case repository" (Contributing_to_EEGLAB.md:191-192) [V].

  ---

  ## 7. Implications for a Cadwell `.ezdata` importer
  1. Minimal deliverable = zip `cadwellio<ver>.zip` unpacking to `cadwellio<ver>/` with `eegplugin_cadwellio.m` (returns `'cadwellio<ver>'`, `findobj(fig,'tag','import data')`, `uimenu(..., 'callback', [trystrs.no_check '[EEG LASTCOM] = pop_loadcadwell;' catchstrs.new_non_empty])`), `pop_loadcadwell.m` (`[EEG, com] = pop_loadcadwell(filename,'key',val)`; `uigetfile('*.ezdataindex;*.ezdata')` + `inputgui` when nargin<1; `com = sprintf('EEG = pop_loadcadwell(''%s''%s);', ...)`), a reader returning `eeg_emptyset` filled with data (uV, chans x samples, single), srate, nbchan, pnts, trials=1, xmin=0, chanlocs(i).labels/.type, event(i).type/.latency/.duration, 'boundary' events with duration for gaps, setname, comments, etc.T0, etc.cadwell.*, then `eeg_checkset(EEG,'eventconsistency')` + `eeg_checkset(EEG,'makeur')`; README + license file. Submit via the "New plugin or plugin update" GitHub issue with the zip.
  2. Via FieldTrip: needs a fieldtrip PR (ft_filetype + ft_read_* + private/) and reaches EEGLAB's *File > Import data > Using the FILE-IO interface* only with the next `Fileio<yymmdd>` snapshot (months). The plugin can also expose `cadwell_fileio_read_header` etc. for FieldTrip users, as mffmatlabio does.
  3. SQLite access is the key dependency decision (Database Toolbox vs bundled MEX vs Java JDBC); it determines Octave support and platform-binary burden.
  4. BioSig offers nothing for .ezdata (only an unsupported EAS/EZ3/ARC stub).

  ## URL index
  - https://github.com/sccn/eeglab (eeglab.m; functions/adminfunc/eeg_checkset.m, plugin_getweb.m, plugin_install.m, plugin_askinstall.m, plugin_menu.m, eegh.m; functions/popfunc/eeg_emptyset.m, eeg_insertbound.m, eeg_boundarytype.m, eeg_isboundary.m, pop_fileio.m, pop_biosig.m, pop_chanedit.m; functions/sigprocfunc/biosig2eeglab.m, biosig2eeglabevent.m, readlocs.m, writeeeg.m; .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/new-plugin-or-plugin-update.md; .github/workflows/test.yml; eeglab.prj; LICENSE; CONTRIBUTING.md; AGENTS.md)
